    <bpmn:process id="W_W5024" name="W5024. Disclosure Governance, Investor-Feedback-to-Management &amp; Board/Committee Reporting" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Board/audit-committee cycle; periodic governance; material feedback; disclosure-event review
Frequency: Periodic (quarterly) + event-driven
Volume: ~4–6 board/committee IR cycles per year
Owner: VP Investor Relations / CFO / VP Legal &amp; Compliance (VS-100)
Participants: Governance (VS-36), Legal (VS-100), Compliance (VS-22), CFO/CEO, Internal Audit (VS-21), Strategy (VS-33)
Source: workflow W5024 — Disclosure Governance, Investor-Feedback-to-Management &amp; Board/Committee Reporting</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W5024_LaneSet2">
        <bpmn:lane id="W5024_Lane1" name="VP IR">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5024_Task4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5024_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5024_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5024_Start3</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5024_End7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W5024_Start3" name="Board/audit-committee cycle; periodic governance; material feedback; disclosure-event…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5024_Flow10</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5024_Task4" name="Govern the disclosure/IR function: the disclosure-committee charter, IR policy…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Govern the disclosure/IR function: the disclosure-committee charter, IR policy, the disclosure-controls assurance (W5017), and the IR-function risk register — reporting to the board/audit committee (links VS-36 governance, VS-21 audit)
Responsible (R): VP IR / Legal / Compliance / Audit
Accountable (A): CFO / Audit Committee
Duration: Periodic</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5024_Flow10</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5024_Flow11</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5024_Task5" name="Report investor feedback &amp; market intelligence to management: synthesize…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Report investor feedback &amp; market intelligence to management: synthesize investor/analyst sentiment (W5029), consensus &amp; valuation signals (W5013/W5030), and ownership/activist intelligence (W5010/W5032) into actionable insight for the CEO/board/strategy (VS-33)
Responsible (R): VP IR / Strategy
Accountable (A): CFO / CEO
Duration: Periodic</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5024_Flow11</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5024_Flow12</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5024_Task6" name="Review disclosure events &amp; lessons: post-mortem of disclosure events…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Review disclosure events &amp; lessons: post-mortem of disclosure events (W5019/W5021), control-effectiveness review, regulatory-change tracking (RA 8799/SEC), and continuous improvement of the IR/disclosure program
Responsible (R): VP IR / Legal / Compliance / Audit
Accountable (A): CFO / Audit Committee
Duration: Periodic</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5024_Flow12</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5024_Flow13</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W5024_End7" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W5024_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W5024_Annotation8">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-117 (ensure disclosure &amp; insider-trading compliance.) | - CTL-750: disclosure/IR function board-reported; investor feedback synthesized to management; controls periodically reviewed
Owner: VP Investor Relations / CFO / VP Legal &amp; Compliance (VS-100)</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
